Z||000019||BBBAD GT||07-21-2000||09:23 AM||||80's Boy:  I was out in the garage last night, and found that I still have a Cartech adjustable FMU laying around.  If that paxton kit doesn't come with an FMU, and you can pulley the blower to below 10#, then an FMU would do you OK for extra fuel.  I'm not sure which kind of injectors are in the Fiero (disc or pentel type?), but pentel types (Bosch) don't mind the extra pressure on the injectors, where as disc type are a little more grumpy (I've heard of Lucus disc type actually shutting close under pressure over 70 psi).  I'll email you a pic.<P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||rogergarrison||07-21-2000||10:58 AM||||Im not experienced with blower type superchargers, never had or worked on one. I have a 'smaller' turbo on my v6 with 8-1 compr. Experimenting with wastegate i find i get best response and power at 4-5 lbs boost. Ive turned it up over twice that and I do notice some missfire, shuddering then. Dont know if its same with supercharger but my 2 cents worth. <P>rg||||reg||1
Z||000021||BBBAD GT||07-21-2000||11:27 AM||||Boost from turbos are a little different than a centrifugal blower, because you can get full boost by 2k rpms with a turbo (depends on a lot of things, but easy if you have a 'small' turbo), where as a centrifugal blower will see max boost only at the top of the RPM's, because its dependent on RPM's (along with load).  Thats one argument aganist a centrifugal blower, it doesn't make the low end torque the positive displacement blowers or turbos do, but when you are on the dragstrip and upper RPM's matter the most, then they really shine. <P>Depends on really what you want personally.<P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
